-- title:
--   Flat local extension realising a prescribed algebraic residue extension
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring, and let $K$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over the residue field $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,T$ making $K$ algebraic over it; both $T$ and $K$ are taken in a fixed universe. The assertion is the existence of a type $B$ in the same universe carrying a commutative ring structure, a local ring structure, a Noetherian ring structure, a $T$-algebra structure, and the property that the structure map $T \to B$ is a local homomorphism (it sends the maximal ideal of $T$ into that of $B$), such that three conditions hold simultaneously: $B$ is faithfully flat as a $T$-module; the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $T$, that is $\mathrm{Ideal.map}$ of $\mathfrak{m}_T$ along $T \to B$, is exactly the maximal ideal of $B$; and there exists an isomorphism of $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,T$-algebras between $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,B$ and $K$, the residue field of $B$ being viewed as an algebra over that of $T$ through the induced map.
--
--   This is the algebraic-residue-extension half of EGA $0_{\mathrm{III}}$, Proposition 10.3.1: any algebraic extension of the residue field of a Noetherian local ring is realised by a faithfully flat Noetherian local extension with maximal ideal generated by the image of the original one. It is used to pass to an algebraic (in particular algebraically closed) residue field, feeding the constructions [`IsArtinianRing.exists_isArtinianRing_faithfullyFlat_map_maximalIdeal_eq_isAlgClosed_residueField`](thm.html#IsArtinianRing.exists_isArtinianRing_faithfullyFlat_map_maximalIdeal_eq_isAlgClosed_residueField) and [`IsNoetherianRing.exists_faithfullyFlat_isAdicComplete_isAlgClosed_residueField_atPrime`](thm.html#IsNoetherianRing.exists_faithfullyFlat_isAdicComplete_isAlgClosed_residueField_atPrime).
